[b]Wardrobe - Transmog Your Equipment[/b]

Choose an outfit from a dedicated Wardrobe tab while keeping your equipped items and their stats.

Browse armour, legwear, gloves/wristbands, footwear and weapons. Choose collected appearances or the full look catalog, keep separate day and night outfits, and save three presets. Hide gauntlets, feet or the sheathed weapon. A character preview stays in place as you choose your look, and outfit saves run in the background.

Use mouse controls, keyboard navigation or an Xbox-style controller. Press End to open Wardrobe, or use its character-menu tab. Mod Setting Menu lets you change the shortcut, enable the mod and turn logging on or off.

The Wardrobe tab sits immediately after Inventory. Its six-column grid uses the inventory background, smaller category symbols, game fonts and rarity frames, with a large character preview and compact equipment slots. The game's keyboard and controller glyphs appear beside the actions, with room below them on ultrawide screens. Save and load outfits in separate dialogs. Navigate with the left stick or D-pad, and switch day/night outfits with P or Start/Menu.

[b]Installation[/b]
[list]
[*]Vortex: Install Wardrobe-Transmog-Your-Equipment.zip through Vortex, enable it and deploy.
[*]Manual: Copy Data/WardrobeTransmog into The Blood of Dawnwalker/Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods, preserving the folder structure.
[/list]

[b]Inspiration[/b]
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/237]DawnwalkerWardrobe[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/353]Transmog - Your Look Your Choice[/url] inspired this independently implemented mod.
